  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. The existing 24 tests pass, but none of them covers this case, and I didn't add a test or check the fix against a real renewal.\n\n**Root cause:** Usage records are timestamped in epoch milliseconds, but billing periods are in epoch seconds. `records_in_period` compared the two directly. A period end of about 1.7 billion seconds was treated as 1.7 million seconds' worth of milliseconds, so every record looked like it fell after the period. No records matched, `aggregate_usage` returned 0, and renewal invoices showed quantity 0 for metered prices.\n\n**Fix:** The period bounds are now converted with `to_millis()` before the comparison.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}\n```\n`git status` doesn't list `answer.json`, so it may be gitignored. I didn't check.",
